BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261012T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261012T220000
SUMMARY:The Page Brothers Quartet
DESCRIPTION:Andy and Zack Page were born four minutes apart and have been finishing each other's musical sentences ever since\, Andy's guitar lines and Zack's bass moving through a shared nervous system built from blues records\, old-time singing\, and hard rock all competing for the same airspace in the same house. Tonight they bring the quartet format to a room that suits it: close enough that you catch everything\, strange enough that anything might happen. Steve Davidowski was the original keyboardist in the Dixie Dregs\, played on the 1977 debut Free Fall\, then walked away at the band's peak to tour with Vassar Clements\, and has spent the years since building something he calls Xenobilly up the road in Marshall.
LOCATION:Little Jumbo\, 241 Broadway\, Asheville\, NC 28801
URL:https://littlejumbobar.com/events/1818/the-page-brothers-quartet/10-12-2026
UID:event-1818@littlejumbobar.com
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261013T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261013T220000
SUMMARY:Sanders\, Boyd\, Page & Hall
DESCRIPTION:Four musicians walk into a room carrying everything they have ever heard\, forgotten\, absorbed\, and transformed. Jay Sanders bends guitar melody through angles that seem to arrive from somewhere outside the visible spectrum. Will Boyd moves between reeds and winds and an EWI that opens into frequencies shaped by South Carolina churches and whatever comes after them. Zack Page supplies the gravitational center\, the low mass around which everything else finds its orbit. Alan Hall has been in conversation with rhythm for four decades\, and he approaches percussion less like timekeeping than like an investigation into what lives inside the smallest units of a beat. Together these four build original music in the room\, in the moment\, from attention and instinct and years of accumulated listening.
LOCATION:Little Jumbo\, 241 Broadway\, Asheville\, NC 28801
URL:https://littlejumbobar.com/events/2305/sanders-boyd-page-hall/10-13-2026
UID:event-2305@littlejumbobar.com
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261019T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261019T220000
SUMMARY:Soul Jazz Revival
DESCRIPTION:Five musicians walk into a room and something older than any of them decides to show up too. Jacob Rodriguez carries a baritone saxophone that has absorbed San Antonio heat and Brooklyn basement air in equal measure\, and when he plays\, the reed seems to remember all of it at once. Quinn Sternberg's bass does not merely keep time — it makes a case\, low and patient\, for why time matters. Joe Enright reads the room from behind his kit the way certain people read weather\, adjusting before anyone else knows adjustment is needed. Alex Taub finds the piano's interior geography\, the places between the named notes where intention lives. Andy Page has played Montreux and Japanese jazz cruises and still shows up to the Blue Ridge with something left to say.
LOCATION:Little Jumbo\, 241 Broadway\, Asheville\, NC 28801
URL:https://littlejumbobar.com/events/1809/soul-jazz-revival/10-19-2026
UID:event-1809@littlejumbobar.com
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261026T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261026T220000
SUMMARY:Brian Felix Organ Trio
DESCRIPTION:Brian Felix has been quietly building something in this room\, and Monday nights at Little Jumbo have been part of the foundation. His organ trio — Felix alongside Tim Fischer and Evan Martin — returns with a horn player joining in\, one of three possible voices depending on who's available\, which means the shape of the evening won't be known until it arrives. That's not uncertainty so much as it is the nature of something still becoming. Newer compositions will share space with older ones\, and the group will do what they've been doing here: listening\, adjusting\, finding where the sound wants to go. The creature in the corner has heard every iteration. Come see what this one turns into.
LOCATION:Little Jumbo\, 241 Broadway\, Asheville\, NC 28801
URL:https://littlejumbobar.com/events/1876/brian-felix-organ-trio/10-26-2026
UID:event-1876@littlejumbobar.com
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
